build
# The instrumented tree tools/sanitize-run.py configures. Same reason as
# `build`: a by-product, rebuilt in about seven seconds from nothing.
build-asan
*.log
# ...but docs/ holds ARTIFACTS, not build by-products, and three of them have
# now been swallowed by that one line.
#
# The first two were fixed by adding a negation each: docs/golden-reference.log,
# which docs/handshake/README.md points at, and the rig-session logs a handshake
# lap cites as evidence. Both were caught late -- the rig one because the commit
# adding them staged the .cue and the .json and silently dropped both .log
# files, while the test that reads one kept passing, because the file was there
# untracked.
#
# The third was docs/sample-interrupted.log. Three instances of one shape is a
# rule, not a coincidence: nothing under docs/ is generated by a build, so
# nothing under docs/ should be ignored. This negation is the whole directory
# rather than a fourth name, and sc_artifacts_are_tracked() is what notices next
# time -- a negation only helps a file somebody remembered to add.
!docs/**/*.log
.github/_build
.github/_install
__pycache__/
*.pyc
